# Data Fetching & API Layer

## Layering

Component → domain hook (`useBlogs`) → `*Api.js` (`blogApi`) → [axiosConfig](client/src/api/axiosConfig.js).

Never call raw paths from components or hooks. Never import `axios` from `AppContext` for new code.

## Queries (GET)

Use `useApiQuery` with `enabled` and `dependencies` for parametric fetches:

```js
export function useBlog(id) {
  const { data, loading, error, refetch } = useApiQuery(
    () => blogApi.getById(id),
    { enabled: !!id, dependencies: [id], errorMessage: MESSAGES.ERROR_FETCH_BLOG }
  )
  return { blog: data?.blog ?? null, loading, error, refetch }
}
```

Map payload at the hook boundary: `data?.blogs ?? []`, `data?.blog ?? null`.

## Mutations (POST/PUT/DELETE)

Use `useApiMutation`; pass `() => blogApi.create(formData)` (not hardcoded paths).

```js
return mutate(() => blogApi.create(formData), {
  successMessage: MESSAGES.SUCCESS_BLOG_CREATED,
  errorMessage: MESSAGES.ERROR_CREATE_BLOG,
  onSuccess: () => refetch?.()
})
```

- Build `FormData` in the hook; `axiosConfig` skips JSON `Content-Type` for `FormData`.
- Use `confirmMessage` for destructive actions.
- Call `refetch()` from related queries in `onSuccess` when the UI should refresh.

## API module

Add methods to `*Api.js` using [API_ENDPOINTS](client/src/constants/apiEndpoints.js); export via [api/index.js](client/src/api/index.js).

```js
// GOOD
getAll: async () => axios.get(API_ENDPOINTS.BLOGS_ALL)

// AVOID
axios.post('/api/blog/add', formData)
```

Register hooks in `hooks/api/queries/index.js` or `hooks/api/mutations/index.js`.

## Anti-patterns

- No ad-hoc `useEffect` + axios when `useApiQuery` fits (refactor `useBlog`-style hooks).
- No `console.log` in hooks.
- Backend envelope is always `{ success, message?, ...payload }`; check `response.data.success` in core hooks only.
